{% comment %}
  Loads the post-debrief fidelity corrections.

  Every lp-* stylesheet is shared by all three funnels, so editing one to close a visual gap
  would also edit the page the panel reviewed. That page is the "before" and must stay byte
  identical. So the corrections live in one stylesheet that only this section loads, and this
  section only appears in the v2 template. Two consequences worth the arrangement:

  - The delivered page is provably untouched — nothing it loads changed.
  - Every fidelity fix is in a single file, so the diff IS the audit trail.

  It renders nothing. Placed last in the template so its stylesheet wins ties on equal
  specificity through document order rather than through !important.
{% endcomment %}

{{ 'lp-fidelity.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "LP fidelity overrides",
  "class": "lp-fidelity-overrides",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Loads lp-fidelity.css, the post-debrief pixel-parity corrections. Renders nothing. Present only on the v2 template so the reviewed page keeps loading exactly what it loaded on the day."
    }
  ],
  "enabled_on": {
    "templates": ["page"]
  }
}
{% endschema %}
